    "https://www.lvc.edu/?p=14425": {
      "title": "Walter \"Wally\" Choplick ’12",
      "description": "Dr. Walter Choplick | Lebanon Valley College Skip to global navigation Skip to page content Skip to global footer Find Your Program Programs Toggle Menu Search Website Close Over 100 Undergrad and Grad Programs Select a program type Undergraduate Graduate and Professional Search by Major or Minor No results found. Not Seeing the Program You Are Looking For? View All Undergraduate Programs View All Graduate Programs Close Close Use the + icon on the right to see more links Academics Toggle menu Academics Academics Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate & Professional Programs General Education Academic Resources Study Abroad Student Research Dutchmen First Program Top Links Academic Calendar 7-week Term Calendar Bishop Library Honors Program Registrar Winter Term LVC Online Bookstore Back Admission & Aid Toggle menu Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Admitted Students International Students Military Students Financial Aid & Costs Top Links Transfer Admission Types of Aid Tuition & Scholarship Calculators Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid FAQs Back Student Life Toggle menu Student Life Student Life Health & Wellness Housing Dining Fitness & Recreation Activities & Clubs Top Links Commuter Resources Safety Spiritual Life Student Mentoring Pride of the Valley Marching Band LVC Online Bookstore LVC Gear Shop Back Athletics Athletics Back About Toggle menu About About LVC Traditions & History Mission & Strategy College Leadership Inclusive Excellence Sustainability Initiatives Working at LVC Administrative Offices & Directories Top Links Summer Camps & Community Programming Breen Center for Career and Professional Development Service & Community Engagement Arts and Music at LVC Our Location Reporting Issues & Grievances Host an Event at LVC Back Close MyLVC News Events Offices & Directories Information For: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents & Families Donors School Counselors Give Deposit Now Request Info Visit Apply Search this website Close Home Dr. Walter Choplick Walter \"Wally\" Choplick ’12 Associate Director, Breen Center for Career and Professional Development Email: choplick@lvc.edu Phone: 717-867-6204 B.A., B.S., Lebanon Valley College; M.M., Messiah University; Ed.D., Concordia University - Wisconsin Biography After graduating from LVC in 2012 with a double major in Music and Music Education, Dr. Walter “Wally” Choplick spent nearly a decade teaching 7-12 Band in the Shenandoah Valley and Gettysburg Area school districts. Knowing he wanted to switch to higher education, LVC was an easy choice when he accepted a position as a Career Coach in the College’s Breen Center for Career and Professional Development in January of 2022. “I remembered the welcoming environment and outstanding faculty from my days as an LVC undergraduate and wanted to give back to current and future generations of Dutchmen,” noted Wally. “I am privileged to offer individual advice to help students succeed personally and professionally after graduation.” Wally, promoted to Assistant Director of the Breen Center in October of 2023 and then again to Associate Director in July of 2024, is pleased to report that everything distinctive he experienced as a student remains. “The relationships and friendships I built at LVC continue. It was like no time had passed with the faculty and staff who mentored me as an undergraduate, and I remain close friends with many classmates. Plus, I now get to interact with everyone across campus, to ensure the success of our students. The students who visit my office are highly motivated to succeed in and out of the classroom.” Wally adds a final piece of critical advice: “Whether it’s your first semester on campus or you are a senior, never hesitate to reach out to our team in the Breen Center. You are not alone. Helping our students achieve their goals gives us great professional and personal satisfaction.” Wally has remained a lifelong learner, earning a Master of Music in Wind Conducting and a Doctor of Education in Leadership, Innovation, and Continuous Improvement. He enjoys reading, going to the gym, skiing, listening to podcasts, and, of course, attending musicals. 101 N. College Avenue Annville, PA 17003-1400 1-717-867-6100 Campus Maps & Directions Where to Park Working at LVC LVC Online Bookstore LVC Gear Shop Academic Calendar Bishop Library The Suzanne H. Arnold Gallery Offices & Directories MyLVC LVC LinkedIn LVC Facebook LVC Instagram LVC TikTok Policies & Legal Notices Consumer Information Translate © 2026 Lebanon Valley College"
    }
  },
